<title>COSTA RICA: SOCCER-COSTA RICA BEAT JAMAICA 3-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-COSTA RICA BEAT JAMAICA 3-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Costa Rica beat Jamaica 3-1</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in a CONCACAF final stage World Cup qualifying</p>
<p>match on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Costa Rica - Paulo Cesar Wanchope (32 and 70), Allan Oviedo</p>
<p>(89)</p>
<p>Jamaica - Andy Williams (60)</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>    Standings	P  W  D  L F   A PTS</p>
<p> Mexico		4  2  2  0 12  2  8</p>
<p> Costa Rica	  4  2  1  1  7  5  7</p>
<p> United States     4  1  2  1  7  5  5</p>
<p> El Salvador	 2  1  1  0  2  1  4</p>
<p> Canada		3  0  2  2  0  7  2</p>
<p> Jamaica	     4  0  2  2  1  9  2</p>
<p>Next match: May 18 - Jamaica v El Salvador</p>
<p>Note: top three teams qualify for the World Cup.</p>
</text>
